# --- Lawn watering START (Smart Irrigation -> valve) ---
# Smart Irrigation only computes a duration; it does not switch the valve.
# This automation bridges the duration sensor to the physical valve.
- alias: "Lawn watering: start cycle"
  description: >
    Waters the front lawn at 05:00 for the Smart Irrigation computed duration,
    then turns off and calls smart_irrigation.reset_bucket so the deficit resets.
    SI calculates at 04:00; this runs the valve at 05:00 when there is a positive
    duration AND the last watering was >=2 days ago (deep-and-infrequent watering,
    user 2026-07-13 — deficit accumulates across skipped days). Calibrated
    2026-07-13: zone throughput 13.4 L/min (METER-MEASURED: 67 L in 5 min; was 25)
    and zone maximum_duration raised to 5400 s, so expect ~40-80 min runs
    every other day (~25 mm/week incl. rain credit). run_seconds capped at 5400 s;
    the valve_2 Max Runtime Failsafe (100 min) is the independent hard backstop.
    2026-07-14: valve briefly moved to Tuya Cloud (its ZHA link was LQI 17, dropping
    ~half of all commands), then moved BACK to ZHA once the user relocated the network
    Zigbee coordinator (socket://192.168.0.42:6638) closer to the sprinkler. Measured
    after relocation: LQI 17 -> 100, command delivery 6/6 (100%), actuation confirmed
    in 2 s (vs 8 s via Tuya cloud). Front lawn = switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
    (outlet 1 unused, user-confirmed). Now fully LOCAL — no internet dependency for the
    5 AM run — and the device's own status_2 / irrigation_duration_2 sensors are back
    for verifying a run actually delivered water.
  id: "lawn_watering_start"
  mode: single
  triggers:
    - trigger: time
      at: "05:00:00"
  conditions:
    # Only water if Smart Irrigation computed a positive run time (calc runs 04:00; read here at 05:00).
    - condition: numeric_state
      entity_id: sensor.smart_irrigation_front_lawn_valve_2
      above: 0
    # Master watering switch on. Odd/even-day bylaw check removed 2026-07-11 (not enforced locally).
    - condition: state
      entity_id: input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable
      state: 'on'
    # Deep-and-infrequent watering (user 2026-07-13): only water if the last completed watering was
    # >=2 days ago (47h allows for trigger jitter). The bucket keeps accumulating deficit on skipped
    # days (it is only reset after an actual watering), so each run delivers the accumulated need.
    # NOTE: SI's own days_between_irrigation setting only gates its start EVENT, which this
    # time-triggered automation does not use — hence the gate lives here.
    # 2026-07-14: gate moved OFF this automation's own last_triggered onto input_datetime.
    # lawn_last_watered (set at the end of a successful run). last_triggered is bumped by manual/
    # test triggers too, survives automation.reload, and has no API to reset — so a single 25 s
    # test silently cancelled the next real watering. This helper is settable, so tests are undoable.
    - condition: template
      value_template: >-
        {{ state_attr('input_datetime.lawn_last_watered', 'timestamp') is none
           or (now().timestamp() - state_attr('input_datetime.lawn_last_watered', 'timestamp')) >= 169200 }}
  actions:
    - variables:
        run_seconds: >-
          {{ [ states('sensor.smart_irrigation_front_lawn_valve_2') | float(0) | round(0) | int, 5400 ] | min }}
    # ---- OPEN, verified. ZHA reports switch state only when the DEVICE confirms
    #      (a dropped command produces no state change at all), so waiting on 'on'
    #      is a true actuation check, not an optimistic echo. Retry up to 3x.
    - repeat:
        sequence:
          - action: switch.turn_on
            target:
              entity_id: switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
            continue_on_error: true
          - wait_template: "{{ is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'on') }}"
            timeout: "00:00:45"
            continue_on_timeout: true
        until: "{{ is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'on') or repeat.index >= 3 }}"
    # ---- Never opened: alert and ABORT before reset_bucket, so the moisture
    #      deficit carries to the next run instead of being falsely cleared.
    - if:
        - condition: template
          value_template: "{{ not is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'on') }}"
      then:
        - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
          data:
            title: "🚨 Lawn watering FAILED to start"
            message: >-
              valve_2 never opened after 3 attempts (Zigbee link? LQI was {{ state_attr('sensor.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_battery','linkquality') | default('n/a') }}).
              Bucket NOT reset — the {{ (run_seconds / 60) | round(1) }} min deficit carries to the next run. Lawn was NOT watered.
        - stop: "valve never opened - deficit preserved for next run"
    - delay:
        seconds: "{{ run_seconds }}"
    # ---- CLOSE, verified. Retry up to 4x (closing matters more than opening).
    - repeat:
        sequence:
          - action: switch.turn_off
            target:
              entity_id: switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
            continue_on_error: true
          - wait_template: "{{ is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'off') }}"
            timeout: "00:00:45"
            continue_on_timeout: true
        until: "{{ is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'off') or repeat.index >= 4 }}"
    - if:
        - condition: template
          value_template: "{{ not is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'off') }}"
      then:
        - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
          data:
            title: "🚨 Lawn valve did NOT close"
            message: "valve_2 still reports ON after 4 close attempts. The 100-min failsafe is the backstop — go check the tap."
    # ---- Water WAS delivered (it opened), so reset the bucket even if the close
    #      needed retries — the close alert above is a separate concern.
    - action: smart_irrigation.reset_bucket
      target:
        entity_id: sensor.smart_irrigation_front_lawn_valve_2
    # ---- Stamp the 2-day gate. Only reached on a verified watering: a failed open
    #      stops above, so a missed run does NOT push the next one out by 2 days.
    - action: input_datetime.set_datetime
      target:
        entity_id: input_datetime.lawn_last_watered
      data:
        datetime: "{{ now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') }}"
    - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
      data:
        title: "✅ Front lawn watered"
        message: "Ran {{ run_seconds }} s ({{ (run_seconds / 60) | round(1) }} min), Smart Irrigation calc. Bucket reset."
# --- Lawn watering veto (Hamilton bylaw odd-day + master kill) ---
- alias: "Lawn watering: veto cycle"
  description: >
    Vetoes Smart Irrigation if watering is banned today.
    Checks odd-day parity (house 31) and master-kill input_boolean.
    Triggered by valve switch turning on; either kills it within seconds or
    sends a confirmation notification.
  id: "lawn_watering_veto"
  initial_state: false  # DISABLED 2026-07-11 per user — odd/even watering bylaw not enforced locally.
  mode: single
  triggers:
    - trigger: state
      entity_id: switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
      from: "off"
      to: "on"
  variables:
    is_odd_day: "{{ now().day % 2 == 1 }}"
    master_enabled: "{{ states('input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable') == 'on' }}"
    duration_sensor_entity: "sensor.smart_irrigation_front_lawn_valve_2"
    duration_value: >
      {% set d = states(duration_sensor_entity) %}
      {% if d | is_number %}
        {{ d }} min
      {% else %}
        (duration not available)
      {% endif %}
  actions:
    - choose:
        - conditions:
            - condition: template
              value_template: "{{ is_odd_day and master_enabled }}"
          sequence:
            - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
              data:
                title: "🚿 Front lawn watering started"
                message: "Watering cycle running for {{ duration_value }}."
      default:
        - action: switch.turn_off
          target:
            entity_id: switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
        - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
          data:
            title: "🚫 Watering vetoed"
            message: >
              {% set reasons = [] %}
              {% if not is_odd_day %}
                {% set reasons = reasons + ['Today is an even day — odd-address watering not allowed'] %}
              {% endif %}
              {% if not master_enabled %}
                {% set reasons = reasons + ['Master watering switch is OFF (toggle input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable to re-enable)'] %}
              {% endif %}
              Watering was blocked.
              {% for r in reasons %}
              - {{ r }}
              {% endfor %}

# --- Lawn watering morning report ---
# Daily 07:00 check on last night's Smart Irrigation calc + whether the
# front-lawn valve actually ran. Confirms the auto-watering chain is healthy.
- alias: "Lawn watering: morning report"
  description: >-
    Daily 07:00 report on the Smart Irrigation calculation and whether the
    front-lawn valve ran since 23:00. Catches a silent calc/mapping failure.
  id: "lawn_watering_morning_report"
  mode: single
  triggers:
    - trigger: time
      at: "07:00:00"
  actions:
    - variables:
        dur_min: >-
          {{ states('sensor.smart_irrigation_front_lawn_valve_2') | float(0) | round(0) | int }}
        valve_last: >-
          {{ state_attr('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'last_changed') }}
        master: >-
          {{ is_state('input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable', 'on') }}
        odd_day: >-
          {{ now().day % 2 == 1 }}
        ran_since_2300: >-
          {% if valve_last %}
            {% set ns = namespace(ts=as_timestamp(now()) - 86400) %}
            {% set cutoff = (ns.ts - (ns.ts % 86400) + (23*3600)) %}
            {{ as_timestamp(valve_last) > cutoff }}
          {% else %}false{% endif %}
    - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
      data:
        title: "🌱 Lawn watering status"
        message: >-
          Calc need: {{ dur_min }} min.
          {% if dur_min > 0 %}Valve ran since 23:00: {{ 'YES' if ran_since_2300 else 'NO — check!' }}.
          {% else %}No water needed (or calc/mapping issue — verify).
          {% endif %}
          Master: {{ 'ON' if master else 'OFF' }} | Odd-day allowed: {{ 'yes' if odd_day else 'no' }}.
- alias: "Lawn watering: veto-failure watchdog"
  description: >-
    Belt-and-suspenders alert for a veto FAILURE. When the front-lawn valve
    turns on in violation of the watering rules (even day, or master switch
    off), the veto automation normally kills it within seconds. This watchdog
    waits a short grace period, then pages ONLY if the valve is STILL on in
    violation — meaning the veto did not do its job (logic bug, manual flip,
    or another automation). Catches a veto failure.
  id: "lawn_watering_veto_watchdog"
  initial_state: false  # DISABLED 2026-07-11 per user — odd/even watering bylaw not enforced locally.
  mode: single
  triggers:
    - trigger: state
      entity_id: switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2
      from: "off"
      to: "on"
  actions:
    # Give the veto automation a few seconds to do its job first.
    - delay: "00:00:10"
    # Re-check: still ON and a rule is violated => the veto failed.
    - condition: template
      value_template: >-
        {{ is_state('switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2', 'on') and
           (now().day % 2 != 1 or
            not is_state('input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable', 'on')) }}
    - variables:
        odd_day: >-
          {{ now().day % 2 == 1 }}
        master_on: >-
          {{ is_state('input_boolean.lawn_watering_master_enable', 'on') }}
    - action: notify.mobile_app_cph2655
      data:
        title: "🚨 Watering veto FAILED"
        message: >-
          {% set why = [] %}
          {% if not odd_day %}{% set why = why + ['Today is an EVEN day — odd-address watering not allowed'] %}{% endif %}
          {% if not master_on %}{% set why = why + ['Master watering switch is OFF'] %}{% endif %}
          Front-lawn valve (switch.tze284_8zizsafo_ts0601_valve_2) is ON in
          violation of the watering rules — the veto did NOT block it!
          {% for r in why %}- {{ r }}
          {% endfor %}
